{"duration_api_ms":912235,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c9f83b90-472b-433d-a401-472993e07d06","total_cost_usd":24.286297000000026,"usage":{"input_tokens":286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254407,"cache_read_input_tokens":38317236,"output_tokens":63738,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":26097},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254407,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3369,"cache_read_input_tokens":346746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2168},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":290,"outputTokens":64437,"thinkingTokens":26285,"cacheReadInputTokens":38369564,"cacheCreationInputTokens":348914,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":24.286297000000026,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":143,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. Report below.\n\n## 1. Per-finding summary\n\n| # | Change |\n|---|---|\n| **1** | `lib/http/download.dart`: the dash branch now sets `entry.mediaType = 2`, so a durl→dash entry stops merging/playing from the type-1 layout. |\n| **2** | `download_service.dart`: `damaged` is now `FormatException \\|\\| RangeError \\|\\| FileSystemException` for **both** media types (entry stays in the queue as `failMerge` instead of being marked complete), with a dash-specific toast. `mp4_remux.dart`/`mp4_join.dart`: a 64-bit box header shorter than 16 bytes throws `FormatException` instead of `RangeError`. `Mp4Remuxer._hasMagic` returns false for a missing/unreadable file, so `isFlv`/`isMp4` no longer throw and the missing input surfaces as damaged. |\n| **3** | `deletePage` now walks `downloadList` **and** `waitDownloadQueue`, marks a merging cid deleted, cancels the repair manager and `curDownload`, removes matching queue entries, then deletes the folder and starts the next download. |\n| **4** | `hasDashAudio` is assigned unconditionally from the resolved stream (`audioFileList != null`). |\n| **5** | `LocalPlayer.release` now takes the mirror path; `VideoDetailController` captures it in `_localMirror` when the entry has a `playUri` and releases that, so a playlist advance can no longer leak the folder. |\n| **6** | New `_streamDirPath(entry)` uses `entry.typeTag ?? '0'` (never collapses onto `entryDirPath`), used at both sites; the `oldTypeTag` delete is guarded by `oldTypeTag != null && isNotEmpty`. |\n| **7** | `_onDone(error)` cancels `_audioDownloadManager` (`isDelete: false`, bytes kept) before returning. |\n| **8** | `DownloadManager` emits the initial progress on resume too (`onReceiveProgress(received, expected)`); `_onReceive` records `totalBytes` whenever `total > 0` and it changed, so `-1` is never persisted. |\n| **9** | `_openDocument` gained `mirrored`; `_pickDocument` passes `false` so a single-file pick leaves `mergedPath` null instead of naming a file that is never written. |\n| **10** | `_completeDownload` only inserts into `downloadList` when `path.isWithin(downloadPath, entry.entryDirPath)`. |\n| **11** | `LocalLibrary.checkImport` rejects a follows box with duplicate mids (before anything is cleared) instead of silently collapsing them. |\n| **12** | `MainActivity.copyDocuments`: rename-then-replace — the old file is only moved aside after the new one is ready, and restored if the second rename fails. |\n| **13** | All constructor-default fields in `BiliDownloadEntryInfo`/`PageInfo`/`EpInfo` `fromJson` read as `as T? ?? default`; the swallowed `catch (_)` in `_readDownloadDirectory` now records `lastError` and logs the skipped entry. |\n| **14** | `appTempDirectory()` always returns a named per-app subfolder (mobile included); `clearLibraryCache` skips that folder instead of just `local_documents`. |\n| **15** | `_timeRegExp` digit groups bounded to `\\d{1,4}`, `timeLength` no longer force-unwrapped, and `DurationUtils.parseDuration` uses `int.tryParse`. |\n| **16** | **No behavioural change** — see uncertainty list. Added a comment recording why the FLV path is one chunk per sample. |\n| **17** | Deleted `Type1.fromJson`, `Type1PlayerCodecConfig.fromJson`, `Type2.fromJson`, `Type2File.fromJson` (and the now-unused `iterable_ext` import); added `test/utils/mp4_join_test.dart` (4 tests over the live `joinMp4` path). |\n| **18** | Took the substantive option: `DownloadManager.expectedTotal` compares the resume `Content-Range` total against the saved size and restarts from 0 on a mismatch (wired for the dash video stream and durl segments); `_streamKey`'s doc reworded to say size is *not* compared there. |\n| **19** | `durationMs`/`positionMs` default to `0` in both self-test result maps. |\n| **20** | WebDAV backup deletes the orphan `.tmp` on failure and reports 「备份失败，原有备份未改动」. |\n\n## 2. `git diff`\n\nThe working tree already carried the other fixer's and earlier passes' edits, so a bare `git diff` would bury this pass. The two diffs above (tool output, verbatim) are the complete cumulative diff **restricted to the files I touched** — `lib/http/download.dart`, `lib/models_new/download/**`, `lib/pages/webdav/webdav.dart`, `lib/pages/video/controller.dart`, `lib/plugin/pl_player/view/view.dart`, `lib/services/download/**`, `lib/services/local_{library,player}.dart`, `lib/utils/{cache_manager,duration_utils,flv_demux,mp4_join,mp4_remux,path_utils,self_test}.dart`, `MainActivity.kt`. Nothing of mine falls outside that set. (`test/utils/mp4_join_test.dart` is new and gitignored, so it is absent from the diff by design.)\n\n## 3. Uncertainty list\n\n- **F2** — `_exportFilePath` can also throw `FileSystemException` (e.g. the export folder cannot be created). That now yields `failMerge` + retryable rather than \"complete with no file\"; I believe that is the better outcome but it is slightly wider than the literal \"missing input\" case.\n- **F6** — reachability was flagged hypothesis by codex and I did not re-verify it; the null-collapse itself I re-confirmed in `path-1.9.1/lib/src/context.dart:264-283`. The `'0'` fallback folder name is invented — a foreign `entry.json` with no `type_tag` will now download into a *new* `0/` folder rather than adopting whatever layout that tool used.\n- **F8** — `onReceiveProgress` now also fires at the resume offset. Only `_onReceive` consumes it and it handles that fine, but it is a behaviour change for any future consumer.\n- **F9** — `_pickTree` keeps its phantom `mergedPath`: the mirrored side files are named `<video-base>.*` and consumers derive dir+base from `mergedPath`, so nulling it there would break the comments/subtitle lookup. I only nulled the case the finding names (nothing mirrored).\n- **F11** — I made this a hard `FormatException` in `checkImport` rather than a soft warning, because that is the one place the finding pointed at and it runs *before* anything is cleared. Trade-off: one duplicated follow now blocks the whole restore. Say the word and I'll downgrade it to a toast + proceed.\n- **F14** — this moves `tmpDirPath` on mobile (`<tmp>/` → `<tmp>/LibrePili/`). I checked every `tmpDirPath` consumer and found no FileProvider XML in the repo, but I could not exercise an actual Android share/save-to-gallery. Also, `loadApplicationCache` still sums the whole temp dir, so the displayed cache size will now exceed what clearing frees; fixing that was outside the finding.\n- **F16** — **I made no behavioural change and this is deliberate.** The suggested fix is unsound here: `_write` copies each chunk as one contiguous `setPosition`+read of `c.length` bytes, and `stsc`/`stco` address samples as chunk-offset + cumulative size, so a multi-sample chunk *must* be contiguous in the source. FLV samples are tag payloads separated by the 4-byte PrevTagSize + 11-byte tag header + codec header, and interleaved with the other track — never contiguous. Grouping them would write tag headers into `mdat` and corrupt the sample tables. (The fragmented-MP4 path can group because `dataOffset += size` makes its samples contiguous by construction.) The `onProgress` half of the cost is already nil: no caller passes `onProgress`. A real fix would need buffered sequential reading in `_write`, which is a refactor of shared code.\n- **F18** — the resume check compares against `entry.totalBytes`, which is the *video* stream's size (the audio manager reports no progress); the audio stream therefore gets no size check. A fresh entry has `totalBytes == 0`, so the check is inert on first download. I assumed CDN mirrors of one stream report identical lengths.\n\n## 4. TEST RESULTS\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (test-policy command)\n  command: dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 106\n  passed: 106\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: 150000\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\n`dart analyze lib test` reports 36 issues, all severity `info` (`cascade_invocations`, `deprecated_member_use`, `constant_identifier_names`) in pre-existing vendored Flutter widget copies under `lib/common/widgets/flutter/` and `lib/pages/dynamics/widgets/` — zero errors, zero warnings, and none in any file this pass touched. `dart format` was run on all 18 touched Dart files (only the new test file needed reformatting).","ttft_ms":5143,"type":"result","duration_ms":1196978,"uuid":"8c904895-e6b8-4f23-9c25-67738959c41d","ttft_stream_ms":4812,"time_to_request_ms":539,"first_content_frame_ms":4812,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
